                    "text": "The article\u2019s selective outrage over an $8.5M cut to a niche voucher program while ignoring the $100M boost to WIC\u2019s core funding is exactly the kind of media malpractice that distracts from real progress. The FY26 Agriculture Bill allocates $7.597B for WIC\u2014maintaining critical support for low-income families\u2014while Commodity Supplemental Food Program funding jumps to $425M to ensure seniors aren\u2019t left behind.\n\nFarmers benefit directly from these sustained investments, which prioritize reliable channels over temporary vouchers. The Biden-era obsession with performative programs is over. This administration focuses on structural efficiency, not scattered handouts.\n\nLocal producers win when funding flows through proven systems, not pet projects designed to generate headlines.\n\nThe numbers don\u2019t lie\u2014see how the real winners stack up: https://t.co/zK5fXIrpkp",
